/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - In the ammonia-water system, ammonia is the refrigerant and water is the absorbent; water dissolves ammonia readily, more so when cold.
   - The energy balance of the whole plant is QG + QE + Wpump = QC + QA, and COP = QE/(QG + Wpump) ≈ QE/QG.
   - An absorption plant takes heat at the generator temperature TG, takes heat from the cold space at TE and rejects heat at the absorber and condenser temperature T0, near ambient.
   - COPmax = (1 − T0/TG) × TE/(T0 − TE), all temperatures in kelvin.
   - The same result follows from the second law: with no entropy generation, QG/TG + QE/TE = (QG + QE)/T0.
   - In the lithium bromide-water system, water is the refrigerant and LiBr solution the absorbent.
   - The Electrolux (three-fluid) refrigerator adds hydrogen to the ammonia-water pair so that the total pressure is the same everywhere; it needs no pump at all, only a small heater, and runs silently in hotel minibars and caravan fridges.
*/
