/* book Worked example: Q: An ammonia-water absorption plant has its generator at 120 °C, its condenser and absorber at 30 °C and its evaporator at −10 °C. It must give 10 kW of cooling. Find the ideal COP and the least generator heat. If the actual COP is 0.6, find the generator heat and the total heat rejected to the cooling water (neglect the pump work).
   1. Temperatures in kelvin: TG = 393.15 K, T0 = 303.15 K, TE = 263.15 K.
   2. Engine part: 1 − 303.15/393.15 = 0.2289.
   3. Refrigerator part: 263.15/(303.15 − 263.15) = 263.15/40 = 6.579.
   4. COPmax = 0.2289 × 6.579 = 1.506. Least generator heat = 10/1.506 = 6.64 kW.
   5. Actual: QG = 10/0.6 = 16.7 kW.
   6. Heat rejected: QC + QA = QG + QE = 16.7 + 10 = 26.7 kW.
   Answer: COPmax = 1.51, least generator heat 6.64 kW; with COP 0.6 the generator needs 16.7 kW and the cooling water takes 26.7 kW. The plant reaches 0.6/1.51 = 40% of its ideal COP. */
