/* book exam traps: The ideal absorption COP needs three temperatures: (1 − T0/TG) × TE/(T0 − TE). TE/(TG − TE) is a Carnot refrigerator COP between the evaporator and the generator, which is a different machine. | In ammonia-water the refrigerant is ammonia; in LiBr-water the refrigerant is water. Swapping them is a common slip. | COP below 1 does not mean the plant is badly designed: its input is heat, not work, and the reversible limit at these temperatures is itself only about 1.4 to 1.5. | The heat rejected is QG + QE (plus pump work), shared between the absorber and condenser. Forgetting the absorber's share undersizes the cooling water. | A LiBr-water machine cannot make ice: its refrigerant, water, freezes at 0 °C. */
